The spec re-parses cleanly with the new scenario in place. The update follows the guided mode (Spec Change Guidance `[add_scenario]`): I modified the existing `Collapsible Reply-Context Prompt Body` Requirement in place — extending its persistence paragraph to cover scroll-position preservation and appending one new scenario — without deleting or weakening any existing content.

```json
{
    "specs_updated": [
        {
            "spec_name": "running-flow-console",
            "change_description": "Extended the 'Collapsible Reply-Context Prompt Body' Requirement to cover internal scroll-position persistence of the expanded .flow-reply-prompt body. Added a paragraph specifying that the expanded body's scrollTop MUST survive automatic re-renders (ctx.innerHTML='' rebuilds driven by the 3s detail poll / ws STATUS_UPDATE), persisted as a session-level UI preference keyed by intervention id (state.flowReplyPromptScroll) parallel to the expand-state map, restored only when initially expanded via requestAnimationFrame, and reset alongside the expand state on open/close of #flow-view. Added a new scenario 'Scroll position of an expanded body survives automatic re-renders' capturing the read-without-snapping-to-top behavior and the independence of the scrollTop-restore path from the first-expand scrollIntoView path."
        }
    ],
    "new_capabilities": [],
    "spec_decisions": [],
    "notes": "Guided mode: executed the single [add_scenario] change intent against the existing 'Collapsible Reply-Context Prompt Body' Requirement via a directed Read+Edit on its physical line range. No new Requirement was created (the behavior is a same-domain extension of an existing Requirement), so spec_decisions is empty. No deletions or weakening of existing scenarios; the prior expand/collapse persistence, first-expand scrollIntoView, and collapse-does-not-scroll behaviors remain unchanged."
}
```

